IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-defaults`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`
IMPORT `je21-art04-08-effects`
IMPORT `je21-art09-10-subordinate-powers`
IMPORT `je21-art11-annulment`

-- je21-seat-2-powers-and-effects: the questions a reader of an enactment asks about powers exercised early, what repeal does, amendment of subordinate legislation, the powers of Orders and Regulations, and annulment.
-- Each question takes the facts the reader can state and no reading of a fork: it uses the default in je21-seat-defaults.
-- Where a rule module answers FALSE meaning "this Article does not give the effect", and the Law says nothing about the rest, the exported question refuses and says so.
-- None of these questions is asked as at a day: the deposited texts of the Law do not differ in the Articles they rest on.

§ `Articles 4 to 8 -- powers exercised early, repeal, amendment`

-- src:56 | (1) This Article applies to any Jersey legislation that confers power to –
-- src:57 | (a) make any Jersey subordinate legislation;
-- src:58 | (b) establish an entity;
-- src:59 | (c) make an appointment;
-- src:60 | (d) give a notice or document;
-- src:61 | (e) prescribe a form; or
-- src:62 | (f) do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(1) (src:56-62)
@export Does Article 4 cover this power? It covers a power given by Jersey legislation to make subordinate legislation, establish an entity, make an appointment, give a notice or document, prescribe a form, or do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power in Article 4(1)` @desc What the power is a power to do
      `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation giving the power is Jersey legislation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 4 cover this power?` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` MEANS
    IF `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 4(1) covers a power given by Jersey legislation to do one of the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 covers any other power"

-- src:63 | (2) The power in question may, unless provision is made to the contrary, be exercised at any time after the making of the legislation, whether or not the legislation is in force.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(2) (src:63)
@export May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force? It may be, at any time after the legislation is made, unless provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power in Article 4(1)` @desc What the power is a power to do
      `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation giving the power is Jersey legislation
      `the legislation conferring the power has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation giving the power has been made
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made that the power is not to be exercised before the legislation is in force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` `the legislation conferring the power has been made` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` `the legislation conferring the power has been made` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:64 | (3) However, no Jersey subordinate legislation made under this power may be brought into force before the provision conferring the power comes into force.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(3) (src:64)
@export Is bringing subordinate legislation into force on this day barred by Article 4(3)? It is barred if the day is before the day the provision giving the power comes into force; the answer is true when it is not barred.
GIVEN `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` IS A DATE @desc The day the subordinate legislation is to come into force
      `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force` IS A DATE @desc The day the provision that gives the power comes into force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force` MEANS
    `Article 4(3): bringing the subordinate legislation into force on that day is not barred` `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force`

§ `Article 5 -- what a repeal or expiry does`

-- src:67 | (2) Unless provision is made to the contrary, the repeal does not affect any of the following –
-- src:68 | (a) the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation (including any saving, transitional or validating provision);
-- src:69 | (b) any existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that legislation;
-- src:70 | (c) any amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation;
-- src:71 | (d) the previous operation of the repealed legislation or anything done or permitted under that legislation;
-- src:72 | (e) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to anything set out in sub-paragraph (b);
-- src:73 | (f) any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed before the repeal of the legislation or breach of it that occurred before its repeal.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(2) (src:67-73)
@export Does a repeal or expiry of Jersey legislation leave this thing untouched? Unless provision is made to the contrary, a repeal does not affect the validity of what was done, accrued rights and liabilities, earlier amendments, the previous operation of the legislation, investigations and proceedings, or penalties.
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument that repealed is Jersey legislation; FALSE if nothing repealed it
      `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of it
      ended IS A `How legislation ended` @desc Whether it was repealed, expired, or otherwise ceased to have effect
      thing IS A `Thing a repeal might affect` @desc The thing the repeal might affect
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended thing `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` thing (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended `default reading L9`) `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"

-- src:74 | (3) Any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in paragraph (2) that relates to an existing right may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in that paragraph may be imposed, as if the legislation had not been repealed.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(3) (src:74)
@export May a proceeding about an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, be brought or imposed after a repeal as if the legislation had not been repealed? It may, where paragraph (2) preserves the right or liability.
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument that repealed is Jersey legislation; FALSE if nothing repealed it
      `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of it
      ended IS A `How legislation ended` @desc Whether it was repealed, expired, or otherwise ceased to have effect
      `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is one of the things paragraph (2)(e) or (f) mentions
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended `default reading L9`) `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)` `provision is made to the contrary` `default reading L10`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 5(3) lets a proceeding about, or a penalty for, something mentioned in paragraph (2) go ahead as if the legislation had not been repealed when Article 5 applies, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:75 | (4) Unless provision is made to the contrary the repeal of any legislation does not revive –
-- src:76 | (a) any legislation repealed;
-- src:77 | (b) any rule of law that has been abolished; or
-- src:78 | (c) any other thing not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(4) (src:75-78)
@export Does a repeal bring back something that was not in force? Unless provision is made to the contrary, a repeal does not revive legislation that was repealed, a rule of law that was abolished, or any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect.
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument that repealed is Jersey legislation; FALSE if nothing repealed it
      `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of it
      ended IS A `How legislation ended` @desc Whether it was repealed, expired, or otherwise ceased to have effect
      thing IS A `Thing a repeal might revive` @desc The thing the repeal might revive
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended thing `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` thing (`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended `default reading L9`) `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 5(4) stops a repeal reviving these things when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

§ `Articles 6 to 8 -- re-enactment, amendment, consequential amendment`

-- src:81 | If any Jersey legislation (whenever made) repeals any Jersey legislation and re-enacts any of its provisions, with or without modification, references in any other Jersey legislation to the provisions so repealed, unless provision is made to the contrary, are construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 6 (src:81)
@export Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to the provision that re-enacted it? It is, when Jersey legislation repeals Jersey legislation and re-enacts the provision, the reference is in other Jersey legislation, and no provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation
      `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation
      `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision
      `the reference is in other Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the reference is in other Jersey legislation
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation` `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in other Jersey legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation` `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in other Jersey legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"

-- src:83 | (1) An amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation by a Law does not of itself limit any further amendment or repeal of that subordinate legislation by other subordinate legislation.
-- src:84 | (2) In the case of Jersey subordinate legislation not made by the States, the reference in paragraph (1) to a Law includes Regulations.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 7 (src:83-84)
@export Can Jersey subordinate legislation that has been amended still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation? An amendment by a Law does not of itself limit this; for subordinate legislation not made by the States, neither does an amendment by Regulations.
GIVEN `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the subordinate legislation that was amended
      `the form of the legislation that amended it` IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the legislation that amended it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` `the form of the legislation that amended it` MEANS
    `Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` `the form of the legislation that amended it` `default reading L5`

-- src:86 | (1) The States may by Regulations make amendments to any Law incidental to, supplemental to, or consequential upon, the making of another Law if the relevant periods of those 2 Laws overlap to any extent.
-- src:87 | (2) In this Article –
-- src:88 | “lodged” means lodged in accordance with standing orders;
-- src:89 | “relevant period” means the period beginning on the day a Law was lodged and ending on the day it was made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 8 (src:86-89)
@export Does Article 8 let the States amend a Law consequentially on another Law that was lodged but not yet made? It does where the period from lodging to making of the other Law overlaps that of the Law to be amended.
GIVEN `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the Law to be amended was lodged in the States Assembly
      `the day the Law to be amended was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Law to be amended was made
      `the day the other Law was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the other Law was lodged in the States Assembly
      `the day the other Law was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the other Law was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` `the day the Law to be amended was made` `the day the other Law was lodged` `the day the other Law was made` MEANS
    IF `Article 8(1): Article 8 gives the States power to amend the Law consequentially on the other Law` `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` `the day the Law to be amended was made` `the day the other Law was lodged` `the day the other Law was made`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"

§ `Articles 9 and 10 -- what a power to make subordinate legislation carries`

-- src:91 | (1) Where any Jersey legislation (whenever made) confers a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation, unless provision is made to the contrary, the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace the legislation made that is exercisable in the same way and subject to the same conditions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(1) (src:91)
@export May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again and again, and does it include a power to repeal, amend or replace what was made? It does, unless provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if Jersey legislation confers the power
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 9(1): the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 9(1) gives these incidents to a power Jersey legislation confers unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:92 | (2) Where any Jersey legislation made after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation, the power may, unless provision is made to the contrary, be exercised –
-- src:93 | (a) to apply generally to all cases or be limited in its application to, or make different provision for different cases or classes of case; or
-- src:94 | (b) to apply generally or be limited in its application by reference to stated conditions, exceptions or factors.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(2) (src:92-94)
@export May a power to make subordinate legislation made after 28 March 2003 apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases? It may, unless provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the legislation conferring the power was made
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if Jersey legislation confers the power
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 9(2) lets a power conferred by Jersey legislation made after 28 March 2003 take these forms unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:95 | (3) The power in paragraph (2) includes the power to make provision about any one or more cases and for the purposes of that paragraph a “class” includes a single case.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(3) (src:95)
@export Is provision about this many cases within the power in Article 9(2)? Provision about one or more cases is.
GIVEN `the number of cases the provision is about` IS A NUMBER @desc How many cases the provision is about
      `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the legislation conferring the power was made
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if Jersey legislation confers the power
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` `the number of cases the provision is about` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` `the number of cases the provision is about` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 9(3) treats provision about one or more cases as within the power in Article 9(2) unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:96 | (4) The power in paragraph (2) enables a provision that repeals any legislation to be brought into force only to the extent of repealing some of its provisions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(4) (src:96)
@export May a repeal made under a power to make subordinate legislation be brought into force in part? It may, unless provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the legislation conferring the power was made
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if Jersey legislation confers the power
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May a repeal be brought into force in part?` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 9(4): a repeal may be brought into force in part` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 9(4) lets a repeal made under a power Jersey legislation confers be brought into force in part unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:97 | (5) Unless provision is made to the contrary, a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation also authorises the making of provision incidental to, supplemental to, or consequential upon that legislation.
-- src:98 | (6) However, the power in paragraph (5) is limited –
-- src:99 | (a) in the case of Regulations, to amending any legislation other than the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 or the legislation giving the power to make the Regulations; and
-- src:100 | (b) in the case of any legislation not made by the States, to amending any other legislation not made by the States.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(5) and (6) (src:97-100)
@export Can this instrument use the incidental power in Article 9(5) to make this provision? An Order of a Minister cannot use it to amend a Law, because the Law is made by the States and the Order is not; it can use it to amend another Order. The answer is refused where provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `the form of the instrument being made` IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the instrument being made
      `the legislation to be amended` IS A `Legislation to be amended` @desc The legislation the provision would amend
      `the provision is an amendment of other legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the provision amends other legislation
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` `the provision is an amendment of other legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` `the provision is an amendment of other legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` `default reading L5` `default reading L6`
    WHEN `Article 9(5) authorises the provision` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Article 9(6) bars the provision` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Article 9(5) does not apply because provision is made to the contrary`
        THEN REFUSE "Article 9(5) gives the incidental power unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what the contrary provision does instead"

-- src:101 | (7) Where Jersey subordinate legislation is stated to be made under any power conferred by any legislation (including this Law) it is treated as being made in exercise of all the powers under which it may be made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(7) (src:101)
@export Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power? It is if it states that it is made under a power conferred by legislation and it may be made under this power.
GIVEN `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it states that it is made under a power conferred by legislation
      `it may be made under this power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it may be made under this power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation` `it may be made under this power` MEANS
    IF `Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation` `it may be made under this power`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 9(7) treats subordinate legislation as made under a power when it says it is made under a power conferred by legislation and may be made under it, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

-- src:103 | (1) The States may by Regulations amend any Law to provide that the power to make subordinate legislation under that Law includes the power to incorporate by reference any technical document (other than legislation from any jurisdiction) that is accessible to the public without charge as it is in force –
-- src:104 | (a) at a particular time; or
-- src:105 | (b) from time to time.
-- src:106 | (2) In paragraph (1) “technical document” means a document that is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product and which is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 10 (src:103-106)
@export Can a power to make subordinate legislation be used to incorporate this technical document by reference? Only where a Law has been amended under Article 10(1) to allow it, and then only for a technical document that is not legislation and is accessible to the public without charge.
GIVEN `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Law that gives the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1) to allow incorporation by reference
      document IS A `Facts about a document` @desc The facts about the document
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)` document MEANS
    `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)` document

§ `Article 11 -- annulment by the States`

-- src:112 | (3) This Article applies to any Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States other than legislation providing purely for the commencement of any legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(3) (src:112)
@export Does Article 11 apply to this instrument? It applies to Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States, other than legislation providing purely for the commencement of any legislation.
GIVEN form IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the instrument
      `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument provides purely for the commencement of legislation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` MEANS
    `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `default reading L5`

-- src:108 | (1) Subordinate legislation to which this Article applies must be laid before the States as soon as practicable after it is made and if the States no later than 3 sittings after the date on which it is laid, resolve that it be annulled, it ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(1) (src:108)
@export Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met? Article 11 requires it to be laid as soon as practicable after it is made.
GIVEN form IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the instrument
      `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument provides purely for the commencement of legislation
      `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made` MEANS
    `Article 11(1): the duty to lay the instrument before the States has been met` (`Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `default reading L5`) `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made`

-- src:108 | (1) Subordinate legislation to which this Article applies must be laid before the States as soon as practicable after it is made and if the States no later than 3 sittings after the date on which it is laid, resolve that it be annulled, it ceases to have effect.
-- src:110 | (a) paragraph (1) may be displaced by any contrary provision in the Law empowering the subordinate legislation; and
-- src:113 | (4) In the case of Jersey subordinate legislation that was made before the commencement of this Part, the reference in paragraph (1) to 3 sittings after it is made is construed as meaning 3 sittings after the commencement of this Part.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(1), (2)(a) and (4) (src:108, src:110, src:113)
@export Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States resolved to annul it? It has if the States resolved to annul it no later than 3 sittings after it was laid; for an instrument made before 28 September 2021 the 3 sittings run from that day.
GIVEN form IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the instrument
      `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument provides purely for the commencement of legislation
      `the day on which the instrument was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the instrument was made
      `the States resolved that it be annulled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the States resolved that it be annulled
      `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of sittings of the States after the date it was laid, up to and including the sitting of the resolution
      `the sittings after 28 September 2021, up to the sitting of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of sittings of the States after 28 September 2021, up to and including the sitting of the resolution; used only for an instrument made before that day
      `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if a provision of the Law that empowers the instrument displaces Article 11(1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `the day on which the instrument was made` `the States resolved that it be annulled` `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` `the sittings after 28 September 2021, up to the sitting of the resolution` `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)` MEANS
    `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect`
        (`Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `default reading L5`)
        `the day on which the instrument was made`
        `the States resolved that it be annulled`
        `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution`
        `the sittings after 28 September 2021, up to the sitting of the resolution`
        `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)`
        `default reading L7`
        `default reading L3`

-- src:111 | (b) the annulment does not affect anything done under the subordinate legislation before it is annulled or limit the power of the body empowered to make the legislation to make further legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(2)(b) (src:111)
@export Does the annulment of subordinate legislation leave alone what was done under it, and the maker's power to make further legislation? It does.
GIVEN `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument has been annulled under Article 11
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does annulment leave alone what was done under the instrument and the power to make further legislation?` `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11` MEANS
    `Article 11(2)(b): the annulment leaves alone what was done under the instrument and the maker's power to make further legislation` `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11`

